# Notes — Desk app core integration design and lab (0519.desk-app 05.01)
Date: 2026-10-31
Recorder: claude-opus-5-5 (Anthropic), the executor this page names as "Claude", in the Claude Code desktop app
State: written FIRST, before the map, the lab and the design. Later sections are appended, not rewritten.

## Disclosure
- This is a continuing session, not a fresh context. Earlier in this session I built 0515 prime-cycle (05.01–05.03), 0517 dependencies and 0518/05.01 (the Colab review adapter, now under Grok's 05.02 repair).
- I wrote prime_cycle.py and prime_support.py. When I map them, I read their code again; I do not rely on memory of writing them.
- I did not build Clerk, return_capture, batch_observe, capture-handoff, prime_review or the app wrappers.

## Inputs
I01. **pack05.01:** 51 of 51 snapshots match their pins and equal live. 49 equal HEAD 960d20c. The other two are uncommitted Prime records: 0416.desk-app/01.002.md (untracked) and 0401.goal/06.01.md (modified so it selects this pack).
I02. **Direction:** 0416.desk-app/01.002.md. The isolation detour is withdrawn. Keep the work-book pack and return route. The first finish line is assignment → retrieve → durable return → Prime retrieves and reviews → next action survives restart. It is for the current Prime first.
I03. **The live route as practised** (read from pages, not README prose):
- Prime writes a `05.NN` batch page with `Executor:`, a source manifest, and a reserved `01NN` member. The reservation names the submitter, the reviewer and the expected outputs.
- The Director releases in chat. The worker copies that release onto the page's Return pointer as `Release:`, then `Claim:`.
- The worker runs `return_capture capture`, then `verify`. It appends `Execution:` with the receipt.
- Prime writes `evidence/prime-reviewNN.NN/REVIEW.md` and the page's `## Review — Codex Prime` text, and edits `0401.goal/06.01.md` by hand.
- prime_cycle's typed review has been used once on live work (0515 actual-use, one work). It is not routine.
I04. **Members today:** 0101–0182 exist. 0181 (Grok-1, 0518/05.02) and 0182 (this batch) are reserved-only. All others have a receipt.

## Early observations (to verify in the lab, not yet findings)
O01. `app/librarian.py where` and `validate` exit 2 on the live record: `assignment_state is not a known state`. Prime wrote `prepared`; the app accepts only waiting, released, running, returned, accepted and stopped. The only worker-facing "what is my assignment" command is down. Read-only run, 2026-10-31.
O02. Prime's 0518/05.01 review exists in evidence/prime-review05.01/REVIEW.md, but that page's Review section still said PENDING when I read it. The review is findable only if you already know the evidence path.
O03. batch_observe on the live 0519 page: `release_raw` is null and ambiguous. The pack template's own line "Release and claim: recorded in the Return pointer…" matches the `Release` prefix, as does the real `Release:` line. Every page made from this template will read as ambiguous.
O04. Submitter labels drift for one model: Claude, Claude Builder, Claude Colab/Builder; Grok-1, Grok Builder 1. An exact-label worker query would miss tasks.
O05. Return band: 17 free numbers (0183–0199). return_capture refuses past 0199 and does not create 0200. At the current rate the band fills in a few working days.
O06. Two job stores exist: the N1NN reservation/capture path (used for every real return) and Clerk queue/claim/return (fixture-only, never used for a real task). The pack says no parallel custody.

## Choices (planned)
C01. **No new store.** The assignment is the batch page plus its reservation. The return is the capture. The review is the page Review text, plus the prime_cycle typed record where Prime uses one. The desk view is derived from those on every read.
C02. **The lab tool is read-only** (`desk_lab.py view`). It enumerates `01NN/reservation.json` files, inspects each member with the pinned `return_inspect`, observes each origin page with the pinned `batch_observe --live`, and optionally merges `prime_cycle read --json`. It derives a per-task state, and who acts next.
C03. **Clerk is not in slice 1.** It would be a second job ledger beside reservations. It is mapped and kept for later routing.
C04. **Demo:** a disposable repository and book, the real pinned CLIs in separate processes, and SYNTHETIC tasks and returns only. Cases: one full loop; missing return versus done; repeated and changed handback; supersedes; stale page after review; interrupted capture; restart.
C05. **Live read-only check:** `view` over the live book, to show it on real records. It writes nothing; the bytes before and after are compared.
C06. **Scope:** writes only to labs/desk-app-integration-pass01, this page, evidence/build05.01, the claim and pointer on 05.01, and capture 0182. No app/, existing lab or core edits, and no Git stage, commit or push.

## Clarification received during the assignment — 2026-10-31
I05. **Director, mid-assignment:** "While completing 0519/05.01, also read: 00.kernel/00.00.10.work/0519.desk-app/06.02.md. The Director selected Prime's return-review cycle as the first real app workflow. Include compute construction of its pages/faces from structured inputs. Start with the templates this loop needs; broader face construction follows. Your existing scope and write boundaries remain unchanged."
- Read: 0519.desk-app/06.02.md (sha256 6c313ceb…68f4) and its decision 0416.desk-app/06.04.md (sha256 00ba3e61…cad). Acknowledged here, and in DESIGN and the return.
- Neither page was in pack05.01. Both are read as source clarifications. They are not new pins and grant no write.

C07. **Construction joins the lab.** The first workflow is Prime reviewing one builder return. The records the loop hand-types today are:
- (a) the batch page's Return-pointer lines (Release, Claim, Execution with the receipt);
- (b) the page's Review section, plus Prime's REVIEW.md;
- (c) the batch page itself, built from an assignment spec.

prime_cycle already constructs REVIEW.md from a structured record, so that one exists. The lab adds a small template renderer for (a), (b) and (c):
- It writes into disposable books only.
- It may only replace a declared placeholder, or append inside a declared section.
- Any other byte change, including an unexplained removal, is refused.
- The model supplies only the judgment text.
- Construction is never a release or an approval.

